WEBVTT


00:00:47.940 --> 00:00:50.524
Neal?


00:00:50.525 --> 00:00:53.693
Neal, come on, wake up.


00:00:53.694 --> 00:00:55.237
Hey, come on, kid, get up.


00:00:55.238 --> 00:00:56.446
We're almost home.


00:01:12.753 --> 00:01:15.796
How long was I out?


00:01:15.797 --> 00:01:17.215
All the way from the airport,


00:01:17.216 --> 00:01:21.466
about three hours.


00:01:21.467 --> 00:01:26.467
What, didn't you sleep
last night?


00:01:26.764 --> 00:01:29.473
Looks about the same around here.


00:01:29.474 --> 00:01:31.183
Yeah,yeah.


00:01:31.184 --> 00:01:33.394
<i>The, um...</i>


00:01:33.395 --> 00:01:36.813
snow just all came off last week.


00:01:36.814 --> 00:01:39.273
It was real nice.
You would've...


00:01:39.274 --> 00:01:41.317
You would've liked it.


00:01:41.318 --> 00:01:44.279
Yeah.


00:01:44.280 --> 00:01:49.277
Too bad I had to miss it then.


00:01:53.996 --> 00:01:56.081
<i>So I guess it's a lot, uh...</i>


00:01:56.082 --> 00:01:59.583
a lot warmer in Florida, huh?


00:01:59.584 --> 00:02:04.583
Depends on
what you mean by warm.


00:02:04.754 --> 00:02:08.423
See you still got
that mumbling thing.


00:02:08.424 --> 00:02:10.758
I don't know.


00:02:10.759 --> 00:02:15.759
You see, Aunt Sara
didn't seem to care if I talked or not.


00:02:19.309 --> 00:02:22.351
Actually, Sara cared a lot.


00:02:22.352 --> 00:02:24.103
Could've fooled me.


00:02:24.104 --> 00:02:26.688
Really?
Really


00:02:26.689 --> 00:02:29.274
You know, kid,
when someone takes your ass in


00:02:29.275 --> 00:02:31.902
and doesn't kick it out
after two years,


00:02:31.903 --> 00:02:35.196
that's 'cause
they actually give a shit.


00:02:35.197 --> 00:02:38.282
And she didn't want you gone,


00:02:38.283 --> 00:02:41.117
if that's what you think,
either, okay?


00:02:41.118 --> 00:02:46.118
It's 'cause the new lady
wants to meet me, right?


00:02:49.293 --> 00:02:51.919
So you did read
the letters I sent you then.


00:02:51.920 --> 00:02:56.918
Yeah.


00:02:57.550 --> 00:03:01.552
Well, I didn't know one way
or the other, you know.


00:03:01.553 --> 00:03:04.596
Response would have been nice.


00:03:04.597 --> 00:03:09.595
I had some,
but they weren't very nice.


00:03:14.897 --> 00:03:18.649
What does Paulie think of her?


00:03:18.650 --> 00:03:21.778
Paulie thinks the world of her.


00:03:21.779 --> 00:03:25.614
Which is one of the reasons
why I decided


00:03:25.615 --> 00:03:28.366
to move forward with her.


00:03:28.367 --> 00:03:33.366
And one of the big reasons
why she wants to get to know you.


00:03:34.914 --> 00:03:39.913
How is Paulie?


00:03:44.214 --> 00:03:46.297
He's fine.


00:03:46.298 --> 00:03:51.297
He's good.


00:04:11.027 --> 00:04:13.612
- Aw, shit.
- Dad?


00:04:13.613 --> 00:04:17.115
I'm sorry. Come on.


00:04:17.116 --> 00:04:22.115
It's gonna be all right.
Come on.


00:04:24.123 --> 00:04:27.624
- Hey.


00:04:27.625 --> 00:04:30.544
It was Angela's idea.


00:04:30.545 --> 00:04:31.836
I'm gonna love her.


00:04:31.837 --> 00:04:33.629
Hey, come on, this is important
to her, all right?


00:04:33.630 --> 00:04:35.006
So just try and remember
what a smile is


00:04:35.007 --> 00:04:37.340
and slap it on your face
for a few minutes, please?


00:04:37.341 --> 00:04:39.176
Ohh!


00:04:41.053 --> 00:04:43.470
Oh, my! Oh, my!


00:04:43.471 --> 00:04:47.224
Oh, so nice
to finally meet you, honey!


00:04:47.225 --> 00:04:48.599
This is Angela, obviously.


00:04:48.601 --> 00:04:50.351
Oh, welcome home.


00:04:50.352 --> 00:04:51.602
I'm Angela.


00:04:51.603 --> 00:04:53.687
Oh, so nice to see you.


00:04:53.688 --> 00:04:55.148
You know,
you must be very hungry.


00:04:55.149 --> 00:04:57.190
You want something to eat,
something to drink?


00:04:57.191 --> 00:04:59.234
<i>I mean, I've made plenty of...</i>


00:05:16.207 --> 00:05:18.709
...in person.
You really are a cutie!


00:05:18.710 --> 00:05:20.626
- Oh!
- Where's Paulie?


00:05:20.627 --> 00:05:22.421
Yeah, where is
your youngest, Hausman?


00:05:22.422 --> 00:05:24.338
I figured he'd be out here
dancing for joy to have Neal back.


00:05:24.339 --> 00:05:26.382
<i>Oh. Uh, well,
you know, Paul's, uh...</i>


00:05:26.383 --> 00:05:27.799
Taking a nap, actually.


00:05:27.800 --> 00:05:29.384
Yeah, he's had a little fever recently,


00:05:29.385 --> 00:05:31.093
and he's just getting over it.


00:05:31.094 --> 00:05:33.804
You know, we just want
to keep him rested for school tomorrow.


00:05:33.805 --> 00:05:36.891
Hey, Neal, you remember me, right?


00:05:36.892 --> 00:05:38.560
Mr. Evans.


00:05:38.561 --> 00:05:40.351
Hey, kept an eye on your dad


00:05:40.352 --> 00:05:41.812
while you were staying
at your aunt's.


00:05:41.813 --> 00:05:43.354
Made sure he didn't
get into any trouble.


00:05:43.355 --> 00:05:45.023
Are you sure about that?


00:05:45.024 --> 00:05:47.442
I think he snuck in a new wife
when you weren't looking.


00:05:48.651 --> 00:05:53.651
Yeah, anyway, you remember my boys,
Richard and Roger?


00:05:55.198 --> 00:05:57.117
Hey, guys.


00:05:57.118 --> 00:05:58.493
They've been talking
nonstop about you


00:05:58.493 --> 00:06:00.453
ever since they heard
you were coming back.


00:06:00.454 --> 00:06:03.288
Hey, we would love to have you over
for our own little welcome back.


00:06:03.289 --> 00:06:04.998
You know, you and your brother
can come over for dinner,


00:06:04.999 --> 00:06:06.248
you can stay the night,
we'll hang out.


00:06:06.249 --> 00:06:09.251
- It'll be great.
- Thanks.


00:06:09.252 --> 00:06:10.543
I'm gonna go tell Paulie.


00:06:10.544 --> 00:06:11.837
All right, great.


00:06:11.838 --> 00:06:13.130
Great to see you...


00:06:13.131 --> 00:06:18.129
Neal.


00:06:24.140 --> 00:06:29.139
Neal?


00:06:30.395 --> 00:06:34.356
Hey, Cara.


00:06:34.357 --> 00:06:37.441
I'm sorry I left
without saying good-bye.


00:06:37.442 --> 00:06:38.734
We just left, like, overnight.


00:06:38.735 --> 00:06:40.861
It's okay.


00:06:40.862 --> 00:06:43.572
I'm sorry I never got
the chance to say sorry


00:06:43.573 --> 00:06:47.910
about, you know, what happened.


00:06:47.911 --> 00:06:49.659
Thanks.


00:06:49.660 --> 00:06:51.871
Hey, Cara?


00:06:51.872 --> 00:06:53.372
Gonna marry that nut job?


00:06:53.373 --> 00:06:56.083
You better keep him
away from matches.


00:06:56.084 --> 00:07:00.128
Shut up!


00:07:00.129 --> 00:07:05.128
I'm sorry.
My brothers are idiots.


00:07:05.424 --> 00:07:06.675
It's okay.


00:07:06.676 --> 00:07:09.552
My brother's inside,
so I should go.


00:07:09.553 --> 00:07:12.180
Cool.


00:07:12.181 --> 00:07:17.179
It's good seeing you, Neal.


00:07:30.947 --> 00:07:35.946
It's gorgeous.


00:09:21.830 --> 00:09:26.830
Paulie?


00:09:28.505 --> 00:09:33.502
Paulie?


00:09:35.551 --> 00:09:40.550
Paulie!


00:09:43.225 --> 00:09:48.224
Paulie!


00:09:52.983 --> 00:09:57.982
Paulie?


00:11:41.156 --> 00:11:42.990
Paulie, Jesus Christ!


00:11:42.991 --> 00:11:45.868
You really scared me, buddy.


00:11:45.869 --> 00:11:47.119
You're not Neal.


00:11:47.120 --> 00:11:48.913
No, of course, I am.


00:11:48.914 --> 00:11:51.040
It's really me, Paulie.


00:11:51.041 --> 00:11:52.249
Prove it.


00:11:52.250 --> 00:11:55.043
Okay.


00:11:55.044 --> 00:11:56.419
Well, Dad, probably flipped out


00:11:56.420 --> 00:12:01.419
when he found out
about these, right?


00:12:11.599 --> 00:12:13.975
It pretended to be you
so many times.


00:12:13.976 --> 00:12:17.103
Paulie, don't talk like that.


00:12:17.104 --> 00:12:22.103
Hey, what the hell's
going on in here?


00:12:23.192 --> 00:12:27.612
God damn it!


00:12:27.613 --> 00:12:29.947
Paulie, what the hell
you doing up here?


00:12:29.948 --> 00:12:30.948
How many times
do I have to tell you


00:12:30.949 --> 00:12:32.074
not to go through these boxes?


00:12:32.075 --> 00:12:33.659
What, 2,000 times?


00:12:33.660 --> 00:12:37.494
- Terry, Honey?


00:12:37.495 --> 00:12:38.996
Is everything okay?


00:12:41.417 --> 00:12:46.416
Sorry, excuse me.


00:12:48.463 --> 00:12:49.505
What'd you think, Neal's back,


00:12:49.506 --> 00:12:51.425
you get to do whatever
the hell you want? Is that it?


00:12:51.426 --> 00:12:52.967
I'm sorry, Dad.


00:12:52.968 --> 00:12:53.968
- Dad?
- What?


00:12:53.969 --> 00:12:55.177
Just hold on a second.


00:12:55.178 --> 00:12:56.553
What do you want?
You want Neal gone?


00:12:56.554 --> 00:12:57.595
You want him
going back to Florida?


00:12:57.596 --> 00:12:58.804
- Is that it?
- Dad, come on!


00:12:58.805 --> 00:13:01.141
What the hell
are you thinking, Paul?


00:13:01.142 --> 00:13:03.642
What's going on?


00:13:03.643 --> 00:13:06.145
This goddamn party's over, Angela.


00:13:06.146 --> 00:13:08.187
I want everybody
out of my house right now.


00:13:08.188 --> 00:13:09.564
Everybody gone! Now!


00:13:09.565 --> 00:13:14.235
Okay! Okay, honey,
just listen to me, okay?


00:13:14.236 --> 00:13:16.403
Move your car.
You're blocking some people in.


00:13:16.404 --> 00:13:18.573
You have to move your car.


00:13:18.574 --> 00:13:23.571
Just take it easy, honey.


00:13:26.037 --> 00:13:30.373
Fine.


00:13:30.374 --> 00:13:32.917
I'm so sorry.
Are you okay?


00:13:32.918 --> 00:13:34.002
Yeah, I'm fine.


00:13:34.003 --> 00:13:36.252
How about you, Neal?


00:13:36.253 --> 00:13:38.840
I'm great, Angela.


00:13:38.841 --> 00:13:41.216
- Listen, um...


00:13:41.217 --> 00:13:44.720
Why don't you, uh,
just take this?


00:13:44.721 --> 00:13:45.762
Get out of the house


00:13:45.763 --> 00:13:47.845
and go and be brothers
for a little bit, okay?


00:13:47.846 --> 00:13:52.847
Be back by 6:00
for dinner, all right?


00:13:59.398 --> 00:14:00.607
Thank you.


00:14:00.608 --> 00:14:03.318
You're welcome, honey.


00:14:03.319 --> 00:14:05.068
Be careful.


00:14:05.069 --> 00:14:08.489
Six o'clock!


00:14:08.490 --> 00:14:13.489
God.


00:14:29.466 --> 00:14:31.216
Aah!


00:14:33.220 --> 00:14:35.386
Wow, Neal, you're here!


00:14:35.387 --> 00:14:37.639
That's right, dude.


00:14:37.640 --> 00:14:39.224
I'm here for good.


00:14:39.225 --> 00:14:40.891
Feels like it's been forever.


00:14:40.892 --> 00:14:42.892
I know, man. I can't believe
how big you got.


00:14:42.893 --> 00:14:47.313
I thought you were gonna be
a midget the rest of your life.


00:14:47.314 --> 00:14:51.525
So how was Florida
with Aunt Sara?


00:14:51.526 --> 00:14:54.277
Aunt Sara home-schooled me
and put me in therapy,


00:14:54.278 --> 00:14:58.280
so I sat around and listened
to how crazy I was for a while.


00:15:01.243 --> 00:15:02.700
What? I miss something?


00:15:02.701 --> 00:15:06.496
No, it's just funny
how sometimes a crazy person


00:15:06.497 --> 00:15:09.248
is the only one who gets it right.


00:15:09.249 --> 00:15:11.625
Gets it right?


00:15:11.626 --> 00:15:13.293
You're not crazy, Neal.


00:15:13.294 --> 00:15:18.293
You never were.


00:15:34.311 --> 00:15:36.813
You can smoke if you need to.


00:15:36.814 --> 00:15:38.232
I can't smoke in here.


00:15:38.233 --> 00:15:42.068
No, I just mean around me.
I don't mind.


00:15:42.069 --> 00:15:45.487
Thanks.


00:15:45.488 --> 00:15:47.114
I think I'm gonna quit.


00:15:47.115 --> 00:15:52.114
I have enough problems already.


00:15:54.078 --> 00:15:55.787
I really missed this.


00:15:55.788 --> 00:15:58.498
You know,
this is the coolest place in town.


00:15:58.499 --> 00:16:03.498
Well, what did you miss more,
this place or me?


00:16:04.379 --> 00:16:05.587
You jerk.


00:16:05.588 --> 00:16:09.132
I was just about to say you.


00:16:09.133 --> 00:16:12.218
Hey, guys, how's it going?


00:16:12.219 --> 00:16:14.303
Hi.


00:16:14.304 --> 00:16:19.303
Hi. Haven't seen you in forever.


00:16:22.270 --> 00:16:25.938
Thought my best customer
left for another diner.


00:16:25.939 --> 00:16:28.357
Well, um, there isn't one.


00:16:28.358 --> 00:16:29.399
This is the best in town.


00:16:29.400 --> 00:16:31.775
Listen to that.


00:16:31.776 --> 00:16:33.945
So, you used to get the Reuben?


00:16:33.946 --> 00:16:36.740
- Uh-huh.
- Two, please.


00:16:36.741 --> 00:16:40.700
Right on it.


00:16:40.701 --> 00:16:42.911
So you have a girlfriend?


00:16:42.912 --> 00:16:44.787
No, no.


00:16:44.788 --> 00:16:45.997
You sure?


00:16:45.998 --> 00:16:48.999
I mean, there's gotta be
like ten girls after you right now.


00:16:49.000 --> 00:16:54.000
Well, um,
I kind of like this one girl.


00:16:54.963 --> 00:16:59.963
<i>She sits right next to me in...</i>


00:17:06.974 --> 00:17:10.600
Neal?


00:17:10.601 --> 00:17:14.354
Whoa!


00:17:14.355 --> 00:17:15.438
Neal?


00:17:15.439 --> 00:17:16.773
Neal!


00:17:21.110 --> 00:17:26.109
Hey, let me ask you something.


00:17:34.414 --> 00:17:37.998
Have you seen this before?


00:17:37.999 --> 00:17:39.708
I don't want to talk about that.


00:17:39.709 --> 00:17:42.252
It's okay.


00:17:42.253 --> 00:17:43.461
It's just me talking
to you, okay?


00:17:43.462 --> 00:17:48.463
There's nobody else but us.


00:17:51.679 --> 00:17:55.347
I found that sketchbook
a while back, yeah.


00:17:55.348 --> 00:17:58.433
I went through your boxes
a few times


00:17:58.434 --> 00:18:01.894
just, you know, 'cause
it made me think of you,


00:18:01.895 --> 00:18:05.480
- and...
- And you looked inside?


00:18:05.481 --> 00:18:09.566
Yeah.


00:18:09.567 --> 00:18:12.903
Is that what you mean
by saying that I'm not crazy?


00:18:12.903 --> 00:18:16.073
You think that you've been
seeing something like this?


00:18:16.074 --> 00:18:20.660
At night, every night.


00:18:20.661 --> 00:18:22.078
Who knows about this?


00:18:22.079 --> 00:18:23.620
You do.


00:18:23.621 --> 00:18:26.331
Only you would ever believe
it's happening again.


00:18:26.332 --> 00:18:29.375
But you didn't tell Dad? Angela?


00:18:29.376 --> 00:18:32.461
No. Well, they know
I haven't been sleeping,


00:18:32.462 --> 00:18:35.214
but I don't talk about it.


00:18:35.215 --> 00:18:39.135
They just think it's me
missing you or school,


00:18:39.136 --> 00:18:44.134
and I just agree with them.


00:18:45.057 --> 00:18:48.057
And you think
you saw me sometimes?


00:18:48.058 --> 00:18:50.644
It's one of the ways
it tries to get me.


00:18:50.645 --> 00:18:53.479
I remembered you talking
about visions you'd have at night


00:18:53.480 --> 00:18:57.149
and Dad saying you've
got an overactive imagination.


00:18:57.150 --> 00:19:00.109
Why was all my stuff
boxed up in your room, Paulie?


00:19:00.110 --> 00:19:03.362
Well, when you got sent away,


00:19:03.363 --> 00:19:05.698
I got kind of sad,


00:19:05.699 --> 00:19:09.743
so Dad packed up all your stuff
and moved me in.


00:19:09.744 --> 00:19:11.410
He thought it would help.


00:19:11.411 --> 00:19:13.288
Oh, shit.


00:19:13.289 --> 00:19:17.123
Yeah, it didn't.


00:19:17.124 --> 00:19:19.876
So you've been sleeping
in my room this whole time?


00:19:19.877 --> 00:19:24.877
Well, I go in there every night,
but I don't sleep.


00:19:26.175 --> 00:19:29.302
Neal...


00:19:29.303 --> 00:19:34.301
you believe me, right?


00:19:42.396 --> 00:19:47.395
Okay.


00:19:49.278 --> 00:19:51.444
Ooh.


00:19:51.445 --> 00:19:52.529
Phew!


00:19:52.530 --> 00:19:56.282
Paulie, what a mess.


00:19:56.283 --> 00:19:58.951
See, is there anything else?


00:19:58.952 --> 00:20:03.951
Nope.


00:20:35.857 --> 00:20:40.857
Damn it.


00:20:59.253 --> 00:21:00.877
Oh!


00:21:06.467 --> 00:21:07.509
Okay.


00:21:15.642 --> 00:21:16.808
Oh!


00:21:16.809 --> 00:21:18.059
Oh!


00:21:22.940 --> 00:21:26.650
This was really close, too.


00:21:26.651 --> 00:21:27.692
Cara.


00:21:36.284 --> 00:21:38.910
What is it, Neal?


00:21:38.911 --> 00:21:40.120
Two Reubens!


00:21:40.121 --> 00:21:41.370
Best in town, right, big guy?


00:21:41.371 --> 00:21:45.374
Oh, my God.


00:21:45.375 --> 00:21:49.795
Hey, Neal.


00:21:49.796 --> 00:21:51.004
Wow, you've been back
for two hours


00:21:51.005 --> 00:21:52.755
and you're already at Melanie's.


00:21:52.756 --> 00:21:56.925
Heh.


00:21:56.926 --> 00:21:58.260
So how was your party?


00:21:58.261 --> 00:22:00.012
<i>Hey, it was, uh...</i>


00:22:00.013 --> 00:22:02.638
It was not much.


00:22:02.639 --> 00:22:04.557
I mean, it was fine. It was...


00:22:04.558 --> 00:22:08.978
Well, well, well,
if it isn't the firebug?


00:22:08.979 --> 00:22:10.604
You know, I heard that your dad


00:22:10.605 --> 00:22:12.396
had to send you away
to keep you out of jail.


00:22:12.397 --> 00:22:14.357
Yeah, didn't something
happen to your mom?


00:22:14.358 --> 00:22:18.776
Did you do that, too?


00:22:18.777 --> 00:22:21.529
You can't believe
everything you hear.


00:22:21.530 --> 00:22:24.532
He got sent away
to protect him from me.


00:22:24.533 --> 00:22:29.532
That's right,
I'm his brother, Paulie.


00:22:29.537 --> 00:22:31.787
I don't remember
what happened that night.


00:22:31.788 --> 00:22:33.998
When I came to
the next morning,


00:22:33.999 --> 00:22:35.917
he was halfway
across the country,


00:22:35.918 --> 00:22:39.502
and I was in a straitjacket.


00:22:39.503 --> 00:22:42.672
What the hell are you talking about?
You're like three.


00:22:42.673 --> 00:22:47.672
Mm-hmm.
That's how I get away with it.


00:22:48.888 --> 00:22:50.721
Let's get outta here.


00:22:52.098 --> 00:22:54.015
You seem like you came
out of everything okay.


00:22:54.016 --> 00:22:59.015
Better than ever, baby.


00:22:59.104 --> 00:23:02.521
Wow.
So, Neal, sorry about that.


00:23:02.522 --> 00:23:04.775
I'll see you around, I guess.


00:23:04.776 --> 00:23:09.774
Yeah.


00:24:25.636 --> 00:24:28.886
So...


00:24:28.887 --> 00:24:33.558
from the foot of the bed
or the side, most often?


00:24:33.559 --> 00:24:36.643
Definitely the side.


00:24:36.644 --> 00:24:39.146
Any idea what time?


00:24:39.147 --> 00:24:40.896
Not really.


00:24:40.897 --> 00:24:45.897
<i>It's when it's dark and late...</i>


00:24:45.986 --> 00:24:50.654
really late.


00:24:50.655 --> 00:24:53.158
Any contact?


00:24:53.159 --> 00:24:54.201
What do you mean?


00:24:54.202 --> 00:24:59.199
Like talking, messages, or...?


00:25:00.205 --> 00:25:04.042
I don't think so.


00:25:04.043 --> 00:25:07.295
What does it do?


00:25:07.296 --> 00:25:10.880
It reaches.


00:25:28.646 --> 00:25:31.315
Dinner, boys.


00:25:31.316 --> 00:25:36.315
Come on.


00:25:39.072 --> 00:25:40.280
It's very good, dear.


00:25:40.281 --> 00:25:42.282
I see the salad is very popular.


00:25:42.283 --> 00:25:43.950
- It is.
- Mm-hmm.


00:25:43.951 --> 00:25:46.201
I cut mean vegetables.


00:25:48.456 --> 00:25:52.040
Oh. Isn't this wonderful?


00:25:52.041 --> 00:25:55.001
We're finally all here.


00:25:55.002 --> 00:25:58.087
So where did you
wind up going?


00:25:59.090 --> 00:26:00.631
Oh!


00:26:00.632 --> 00:26:01.965
Stop that.


00:26:01.966 --> 00:26:03.425
Melanie's.


00:26:03.426 --> 00:26:04.760
I love that place.


00:26:04.761 --> 00:26:07.136
It's such a great idea.


00:26:07.137 --> 00:26:08.763
Is that where
your appetite went, Neal?


00:26:08.764 --> 00:26:10.931
- Paulie? Stop that.
- Enough.


00:26:10.932 --> 00:26:12.265
You're not tossing food.


00:26:12.266 --> 00:26:17.266
No, I didn't eat
my sandwich, either.


00:26:17.729 --> 00:26:22.399
You want me to cook
you something?


00:26:22.400 --> 00:26:23.983
- You sure?
- No, no.


00:26:23.984 --> 00:26:25.443
No, like a soufflé, you know.


00:26:26.487 --> 00:26:28.529
I'd like to see that.


00:26:28.530 --> 00:26:33.530
So where's Neal gonna sleep?


00:26:34.285 --> 00:26:36.577
Well, Angela and I
talked about that a little bit,


00:26:36.578 --> 00:26:41.456
and, um, you know,
Paulie's in your old room,


00:26:41.457 --> 00:26:44.084
so we thought maybe
you'd be okay


00:26:44.085 --> 00:26:46.504
trying something a little different.


00:26:46.505 --> 00:26:48.045
I made a bed for you
in Paulie's old room.


00:26:48.046 --> 00:26:50.173
I hope that's okay.


00:26:50.174 --> 00:26:51.882
Paulie's room.


00:26:51.883 --> 00:26:54.552
That's great, considering that all--


00:26:54.553 --> 00:26:59.551
all my shit is in there.


00:28:41.184 --> 00:28:44.853
So nice to see
many of your happy faces here


00:28:44.854 --> 00:28:47.189
supporting theater in the schools.


00:28:47.190 --> 00:28:50.649
Maybe that'll send
the school board a message, huh?


00:28:50.650 --> 00:28:53.401
Well, you might have noticed
that our turnout


00:28:53.402 --> 00:28:57.571
for this year's school play
is a little light.


00:28:57.572 --> 00:28:59.448
You can thank your parents
for responding so well


00:28:59.449 --> 00:29:01.824
to my original piece I wrote,


00:29:01.825 --> 00:29:06.825
"Barry Bonds:
Hero or Cheater?"


00:29:17.215 --> 00:29:19.967
Undaunted, I'm gonna move on
to my next project,


00:29:19.968 --> 00:29:21.676
which will be a lot of fun.


00:29:21.677 --> 00:29:24.719
We're gonna do "The Crucible,
the Musical," and...


00:30:24.564 --> 00:30:25.855
Wake up!


00:30:25.856 --> 00:30:28.189
Aah!


00:30:28.190 --> 00:30:30.483
Aah!


00:30:30.484 --> 00:30:35.483
Aah!


00:31:05.597 --> 00:31:10.434
Look, I get that you need
some time to readjust, Neal.


00:31:10.435 --> 00:31:12.477
Okay, I do,


00:31:12.478 --> 00:31:15.146
but I got you two
staring off into nothing.


00:31:15.147 --> 00:31:16.315
You're not eating.


00:31:16.316 --> 00:31:19.191
You sure as shit don't care
about Angela's feelings.


00:31:19.192 --> 00:31:21.860
And you know what
I don't want, boys?


00:31:21.861 --> 00:31:26.860
I don't want today
to become every other day.


00:31:27.115 --> 00:31:29.784
We used to be normal.


00:31:29.785 --> 00:31:32.619
Do you remember that?


00:31:32.620 --> 00:31:35.121
We're gonna be again.


00:31:35.122 --> 00:31:40.121
We're gonna be,
but it's up to you boys.


00:31:41.627 --> 00:31:45.004
Paulie?


00:31:45.005 --> 00:31:46.089
Angela and I have decided


00:31:46.090 --> 00:31:47.799
we're gonna keep you
out of school for a little while.


00:31:47.800 --> 00:31:50.175
No. No, no, no,
you can't do that!


00:31:50.176 --> 00:31:51.510
Why?


00:31:51.511 --> 00:31:55.222
Why?
Are you actually asking why?


00:31:55.223 --> 00:31:56.972
Should we ask
all your--your classmates


00:31:56.973 --> 00:32:01.102
who watched you
melt down today why, Paulie?


00:32:01.103 --> 00:32:04.354
Now, look, the--the priority
here is to get you guys


00:32:04.355 --> 00:32:07.315
both back to earth
and back in school in a week,


00:32:07.316 --> 00:32:11.111
and we are gonna do it!


00:32:11.112 --> 00:32:13.904
But before I can enroll you, Neal,


00:32:13.905 --> 00:32:15.697
I need you to do
some things for me, son.


00:32:15.698 --> 00:32:17.740
Oh, yeah? What's that?


00:32:17.741 --> 00:32:22.741
Like grow the fuck up, for one.


00:32:22.996 --> 00:32:26.915
Like become a man!


00:32:26.916 --> 00:32:28.333
You're were only supposed
to go down to Sara's


00:32:28.334 --> 00:32:30.418
for a couple of months,


00:32:30.419 --> 00:32:32.670
but she wanted you there
because she thought it was helping.


00:32:32.671 --> 00:32:34.712
But if two years down there
is not getting you to grow up,


00:32:34.713 --> 00:32:35.964
then I'm gonna do it!


00:32:35.965 --> 00:32:38.216
Your ass is getting a job!


00:32:38.217 --> 00:32:40.342
Is getting a job
gonna make me a man?


00:32:40.343 --> 00:32:42.512
Well, it's sure as shit gonna help!


00:32:42.513 --> 00:32:46.557
Uh, Neal, honey?
I think what your dad


00:32:46.558 --> 00:32:48.099
is trying to say is that


00:32:48.100 --> 00:32:51.893
Paulie needs a role model.


00:32:55.148 --> 00:32:57.566
Are you okay?


00:32:59.694 --> 00:33:01.361
- Neal! Are you listening?
- Yes!


00:33:01.362 --> 00:33:02.987
Yes? Okay, then
what did we just say?


00:33:02.988 --> 00:33:04.280
That I'm still crazy!


00:33:04.281 --> 00:33:05.698
No, that is not
what we just said!


00:33:05.699 --> 00:33:07.199
That's all that anybody thinks!


00:33:07.200 --> 00:33:08.950
I'm not even getting a chance!


00:33:08.951 --> 00:33:10.244
You don't get chances, kid!


00:33:10.245 --> 00:33:11.952
You earn them,
and you're not doing it!


00:33:11.953 --> 00:33:16.953
Well, maybe I should have
just died with Mom!


00:33:22.046 --> 00:33:27.044
You two go to bed.


00:33:33.681 --> 00:33:34.763
Angela's making
you act completely...


00:33:34.764 --> 00:33:37.058
Stop it, Neal.


00:33:37.059 --> 00:33:40.144
Please just stop talking,
all right?


00:33:40.145 --> 00:33:42.562
Now, you two brought
this on yourselves.


00:33:42.563 --> 00:33:44.732
This door's gonna stay locked.


00:33:44.733 --> 00:33:46.523
You gotta go to the bathroom,
you knock.


00:33:46.524 --> 00:33:51.524
Otherwise,
all I want to hear is silence.


00:33:53.114 --> 00:33:58.113
Sleep tight!


00:34:02.497 --> 00:34:03.872
Don't start with me.


00:34:03.873 --> 00:34:05.498
Maybe we should consider
outside help.


00:34:05.499 --> 00:34:07.833
No. We've done that,
and it hasn't done jack shit.


00:34:07.834 --> 00:34:09.334
We are doing this ourselves.


00:34:09.335 --> 00:34:11.462
But something
is going on here, Terry.


00:34:11.463 --> 00:34:13.214
Yes, Angela, there is,


00:34:13.215 --> 00:34:18.213
and we're gonna put a stop to it.


00:34:20.304 --> 00:34:22.763
You sleep with the light on?


00:34:22.764 --> 00:34:25.806
At night, yeah.


00:34:25.807 --> 00:34:27.892
For how long?


00:34:27.893 --> 00:34:32.853
About a year now.


00:34:32.854 --> 00:34:35.690
But it helps?


00:34:35.691 --> 00:34:40.691
Mm-mmm.


00:34:57.794 --> 00:35:01.170
Hey, let's try something,


00:35:01.171 --> 00:35:05.966
you and me.


00:35:05.967 --> 00:35:10.967
Turn the light off.


00:35:16.643 --> 00:35:21.641
Neal, what are you gonna do?


00:35:23.273 --> 00:35:28.272
Hey.


00:35:34.282 --> 00:35:35.323
Hey!


00:35:42.622 --> 00:35:45.291
If we don't make any noise,


00:35:45.292 --> 00:35:50.086
it doesn't know we're here.


00:35:50.087 --> 00:35:54.881
What about when we move?


00:35:54.882 --> 00:35:59.881
Here, let me try something.


00:36:14.941 --> 00:36:18.068
So we don't move,
we don't make any sound,


00:36:18.069 --> 00:36:20.028
it's not gonna try anything, right?


00:36:20.029 --> 00:36:25.030
- Paulie, he's right behind you, man!


00:36:39.796 --> 00:36:41.587
How close did it come to me?


00:36:41.588 --> 00:36:44.216
Um, not that close.


00:36:44.217 --> 00:36:46.635
Still had half the room to go.


00:36:46.636 --> 00:36:49.762
A couple of feet.


00:36:49.763 --> 00:36:52.765
We're all right
with the lights on, I think.


00:36:52.766 --> 00:36:56.016
Yeah.


00:36:56.017 --> 00:37:00.562
Wonder what Angela tells Dad.


00:37:00.563 --> 00:37:02.564
What do you think of her?


00:37:02.565 --> 00:37:05.149
She's kind of cool.


00:37:05.150 --> 00:37:07.610
Seriously?


00:37:07.611 --> 00:37:10.112
Does she even have a job?


00:37:10.113 --> 00:37:12.656
She's a substitute teacher.


00:37:12.657 --> 00:37:14.824
Good for her.


00:37:14.825 --> 00:37:17.618
Substitute teacher,
substitute wife,


00:37:17.619 --> 00:37:21.079
substitute mom.


00:37:21.080 --> 00:37:24.582
She's got it all figured out.


00:37:24.583 --> 00:37:29.583
Neal, you should give her a chance.


00:37:29.629 --> 00:37:34.630
Does Dad ever talk about Mom?


00:37:34.759 --> 00:37:39.759
Never, except
when he'd talk about you.


00:37:41.181 --> 00:37:44.391
Does he blame me?


00:37:44.392 --> 00:37:47.436
He blames everybody.


00:37:47.437 --> 00:37:49.895
<i>' Hey, Neal?
'Hmm?</i>


00:37:49.896 --> 00:37:52.231
Want to see how I get to bed?


00:37:52.232 --> 00:37:57.231
Yeah.


00:38:29.763 --> 00:38:31.264
So I was thinking
about how we'd keep you


00:38:31.265 --> 00:38:33.057
off the floor tonight, Neal.


00:38:33.058 --> 00:38:36.768
I was just gonna
stay up all night.


00:38:36.769 --> 00:38:39.478
Not like I haven't done it before.


00:38:39.479 --> 00:38:42.149
Well, maybe you can
sleep on the dresser.


00:38:42.150 --> 00:38:47.149
I mean, better than no sleep.


00:38:47.696 --> 00:38:52.695
Worth a shot.


00:38:52.700 --> 00:38:57.700
Just run, Neal.
You're gonna make it mad.


00:39:13.092 --> 00:39:15.176
I think I made it mad anyway.


00:39:15.178 --> 00:39:20.177
Well, it's a lot noisier
than it's ever been before.


00:39:21.974 --> 00:39:25.642
It remembers me.


00:39:25.643 --> 00:39:28.562
It's been a long two years, Neal.


00:39:28.563 --> 00:39:32.484
I'm glad you haven't changed.


00:39:32.485 --> 00:39:35.777
What happened to you today?


00:39:35.778 --> 00:39:40.778
I fell asleep in class,
and I woke up screaming.


00:39:41.365 --> 00:39:44.825
Why didn't you
say anything, man?


00:39:44.826 --> 00:39:49.330
Well, 'cause I kind of
like just hanging out


00:39:49.331 --> 00:39:54.330
without talking about screaming.


00:39:57.420 --> 00:40:02.341
You ready to stop screaming?


00:40:02.342 --> 00:40:06.970
Yeah.


00:41:03.183 --> 00:41:04.435
Paulie?


00:41:04.436 --> 00:41:06.770
Paulie! Paulie,
if you're sleeping, wake up!


00:41:06.771 --> 00:41:08.647
Wake up, man,
there's something happening!


00:41:08.648 --> 00:41:11.232
Yeah, this stuff.


00:41:11.233 --> 00:41:12.441
I don't remember this!


00:41:12.442 --> 00:41:14.111
What the fuck is this, man?


00:41:14.112 --> 00:41:16.278
Usually happens
after I've already fallen asleep.


00:41:26.830 --> 00:41:28.122
What's happening?!


00:41:28.123 --> 00:41:30.291
I don't know, Paulie!
Hang on!


00:42:12.869 --> 00:42:15.202
Dad!


00:42:15.203 --> 00:42:16.163
Dad, what are you doing?


00:42:16.164 --> 00:42:17.704
Dad, leave him alone!


00:42:17.705 --> 00:42:19.497
Dad! Dad!
What are you doing?


00:42:21.083 --> 00:42:22.667
- Get off him, Dad!
- Dad, what--


00:42:22.668 --> 00:42:23.668
- Stop!
- Dad!


00:42:23.669 --> 00:42:26.212
- Neal!


00:42:26.213 --> 00:42:27.671
No! Dad!


00:42:27.672 --> 00:42:29.340
Dad, stop!


00:42:29.341 --> 00:42:31.508
Dad! Dad!


00:42:31.509 --> 00:42:33.842
- No, no!


00:42:35.805 --> 00:42:40.803
Aah!


00:42:48.940 --> 00:42:50.191
Does it hurt?


00:42:50.192 --> 00:42:53.653
Mm-hmm.


00:42:53.654 --> 00:42:57.196
Do you want to tell me
exactly what happened, honey?


00:42:57.197 --> 00:43:00.699
No.


00:43:00.700 --> 00:43:02.952
Paulie, you know,
I can put medicine on your bruises


00:43:02.953 --> 00:43:05.078
in the middle of the night,


00:43:05.079 --> 00:43:06.704
but the only way
I can truly help you


00:43:06.705 --> 00:43:11.705
is if I can stop this
from happening in the first place.


00:43:16.129 --> 00:43:20.424
Paulie, honey, I love you,


00:43:20.425 --> 00:43:25.011
and I really want to help you,
but you have to trust me.


00:43:25.012 --> 00:43:27.597
Please trust me.


00:43:27.598 --> 00:43:30.266
Okay, you have two ways
of answering this for me.


00:43:30.267 --> 00:43:32.519
Either you did this,
or he did this to himself.


00:43:32.520 --> 00:43:35.104
- Which one is it?
- No.


00:43:35.105 --> 00:43:37.063
Which answer, Neal?


00:43:37.064 --> 00:43:38.941
<i>Which answer is gonna
make us less miserable?</i>


00:43:38.942 --> 00:43:39.983
You don't really think


00:43:39.984 --> 00:43:43.861
that I would ever
do that to him, do you?


00:43:43.862 --> 00:43:44.903
So he did it to himself?


00:43:44.904 --> 00:43:46.447
I didn't say that.


00:43:46.448 --> 00:43:47.488
God damn it, Neal!


00:43:47.489 --> 00:43:49.950
Knock this shit off, please!


00:43:49.951 --> 00:43:52.034
'Cause I don't think
you two can survive another day!


00:43:52.035 --> 00:43:56.163
I don't think I can survive
another day of this!


00:43:56.164 --> 00:43:59.708
I know.


00:43:59.709 --> 00:44:03.419
This is not the way to protect
your little brother.


00:44:03.420 --> 00:44:06.296
You know, he doesn't need you
making excuses for him.


00:44:06.297 --> 00:44:10.382
He needs you being a man,
standing up for him.


00:44:10.383 --> 00:44:15.384
I'm trying.


00:44:17.808 --> 00:44:19.933
Dad thinks you did it.


00:44:19.934 --> 00:44:21.852
Really?


00:44:21.853 --> 00:44:23.687
Angela thinks you did it.


00:44:23.688 --> 00:44:28.686
She does?


00:44:29.191 --> 00:44:33.318
If she says that to my face,
I'm gonna call her a bitch to hers.


00:44:33.319 --> 00:44:38.319
Well, then that'd be
the first time you talked to her.


00:44:41.369 --> 00:44:44.620
Did it hurt when it grabbed you?


00:44:44.621 --> 00:44:46.330
<i>No, it...</i>


00:44:46.331 --> 00:44:48.332
It felt worse.


00:44:48.333 --> 00:44:50.625
Like what'd it feel like?


00:44:50.626 --> 00:44:53.044
It was cold and...
and numb,


00:44:53.046 --> 00:44:54.920
and it felt like I was...


00:44:54.921 --> 00:44:58.299
Falling asleep?


00:44:58.300 --> 00:45:00.051
Yeah.


00:45:00.052 --> 00:45:04.388
Jesus Christ.


00:45:04.389 --> 00:45:06.722
Okay, boys, it's late.


00:45:06.723 --> 00:45:11.724
Let's try this again, shall we?


00:45:14.604 --> 00:45:18.816
Come on, honey,
let's get you back to bed.


00:45:18.817 --> 00:45:21.026
Honey, come here.


00:45:21.027 --> 00:45:23.029
I'm really worried about you.


00:45:23.030 --> 00:45:25.071
How can I make this better?


00:45:25.072 --> 00:45:26.572
Can I have my sleeping bag?


00:45:26.573 --> 00:45:27.532
Sure, I'll go get your sleeping...


00:45:27.533 --> 00:45:29.909
No. Paulie's sleeping in a bed


00:45:29.910 --> 00:45:31.577
like a normal person,


00:45:31.578 --> 00:45:35.956
and this door is staying locked.


00:45:35.957 --> 00:45:37.748
The sooner you two
get past this phase...


00:45:39.084 --> 00:45:40.625
The sooner we can
go on living our lives.


00:45:40.626 --> 00:45:41.628
What are you doing?


00:45:41.629 --> 00:45:42.878
What am I doing?


00:45:42.879 --> 00:45:44.962
Normal people sleep in the dark!


00:45:44.963 --> 00:45:46.090
So is he!


00:45:46.091 --> 00:45:47.382
It's a little extreme, Terry.


00:45:47.383 --> 00:45:52.381
Come on, please?
Come on.


00:46:37.843 --> 00:46:42.841
Neal.


00:46:45.723 --> 00:46:50.722
Come on.


00:47:44.732 --> 00:47:47.859
Boys?


00:47:47.860 --> 00:47:51.862
Paulie? Neal?


00:47:51.863 --> 00:47:55.198
Wake up.


00:47:55.199 --> 00:47:58.576
Good morning.


00:47:58.577 --> 00:48:00.578
You okay?


00:48:00.579 --> 00:48:05.578
Yeah, Dad, we're both fine.


00:48:05.916 --> 00:48:07.124
<i>Okay, Well, it's...</i>


00:48:07.125 --> 00:48:10.084
It's breakfast time.


00:48:10.085 --> 00:48:15.086
Come on.


00:48:15.841 --> 00:48:17.008
I know. Thank you, Sam.


00:48:17.009 --> 00:48:19.135
I really appreciate it.


00:48:19.136 --> 00:48:20.677
Yes, I will.


00:48:20.678 --> 00:48:25.678
Thanks. Bye-bye.


00:48:27.184 --> 00:48:28.642
They understand.


00:48:28.643 --> 00:48:32.145
They're not happy,
but they...they get it.


00:48:32.146 --> 00:48:33.940
I'm sorry, Ang.


00:48:33.941 --> 00:48:38.692
It's okay, honey.
It's not your fault.


00:48:40.987 --> 00:48:44.530
I found Neal in Paulie's room
this morning.


00:48:44.531 --> 00:48:46.741
- What?
- Snuck in.


00:48:46.742 --> 00:48:48.618
Oh, my gosh.


00:48:48.619 --> 00:48:51.329
At least they didn't
kill each other.


00:48:51.330 --> 00:48:55.250
Oh, honey, I'm so sorry.


00:48:55.251 --> 00:49:00.248
I swear to God, Ang,
I have no idea what to do.


00:49:03.756 --> 00:49:07.175
Did Dad tell you
about Mom's grave?


00:49:07.176 --> 00:49:11.262
One of his letters
had pictures of it.


00:49:11.263 --> 00:49:16.262
Yeah, well, she's not there.


00:49:21.356 --> 00:49:26.354
No fuckin' way.


00:49:26.526 --> 00:49:28.609
I wanted her to stay here,


00:49:28.610 --> 00:49:33.489
and Dad said it was okay
as long as he didn't see it.


00:49:33.490 --> 00:49:38.489
So I keep it in here.


00:50:05.808 --> 00:50:09.810
You remember Mom
staying in the house


00:50:09.811 --> 00:50:14.566
after the fire reached
the living room?


00:50:14.567 --> 00:50:18.234
That night...


00:50:18.235 --> 00:50:19.611
I begged her to stay with me


00:50:19.612 --> 00:50:22.114
so she could see
what was under the bed.


00:50:22.115 --> 00:50:27.034
She did, and...


00:50:27.035 --> 00:50:32.036
she died because she believed me.


00:50:32.497 --> 00:50:37.497
She was protecting us.


00:50:39.795 --> 00:50:42.213
I miss her.


00:51:10.030 --> 00:51:14.532
Look, you gotta hold it
from the side, too.


00:51:14.533 --> 00:51:16.075
Keep your finger
on the trigger.


00:51:16.076 --> 00:51:17.994
Keep it steady and push forward
with your back hand.


00:51:17.995 --> 00:51:21.038
In.


00:51:21.039 --> 00:51:23.457
You'd have to be pretty close
to hurt it with this, right?


00:51:23.458 --> 00:51:26.376
Well, yeah.


00:51:26.377 --> 00:51:27.502
We'd have to get closer


00:51:27.503 --> 00:51:32.503
than we've ever been
before sooner or later.


00:51:44.433 --> 00:51:49.433
What makes you think
we can kill it?


00:51:49.605 --> 00:51:52.564
I think it's afraid of us,


00:51:52.565 --> 00:51:55.900
and it wouldn't be afraid of anything
if it couldn't die, Paul.


00:51:55.901 --> 00:52:00.901
Would you be?


00:52:03.074 --> 00:52:07.744
We're something this thing
has never dealt with before.


00:52:07.745 --> 00:52:12.744
What?


00:52:17.087 --> 00:52:21.756
We're brothers.


00:52:21.757 --> 00:52:24.842
Oh, shit.


00:52:24.843 --> 00:52:26.217
Whoa! Whoa! Whoa!


00:52:26.218 --> 00:52:29.011
Uh, Neal, dear?


00:52:29.012 --> 00:52:31.638
Let's leave that alone
for the time being.


00:52:31.639 --> 00:52:33.892
Dad taught me to use it before.


00:52:33.893 --> 00:52:37.186
Well, he's not here
right now, so, uh,


00:52:37.187 --> 00:52:38.270
put it down.


00:52:38.271 --> 00:52:39.563
I'll be fine.


00:52:39.564 --> 00:52:42.356
Put it down,


00:52:42.357 --> 00:52:46.610
please.


00:52:50.448 --> 00:52:55.448
Come on, pal.


00:52:58.288 --> 00:52:59.371
Paulie?


00:52:59.372 --> 00:53:01.539
Sweetheart,


00:53:01.540 --> 00:53:03.248
please tell me what's going on.


00:53:03.249 --> 00:53:04.709
It's not a big deal.


00:53:04.710 --> 00:53:06.460
Well, if you can just tell me
a little bit, honey,


00:53:06.461 --> 00:53:11.214
maybe I can, I don't know,
somehow help you?


00:53:11.215 --> 00:53:16.215
If you want to help him,
stay out of his way.


00:54:03.092 --> 00:54:04.926
It looks pretty good in there.


00:54:04.927 --> 00:54:09.927
Yeah, not bad for two hours
of sleep between us.


00:54:27.571 --> 00:54:30.658
We're okay.


00:54:30.659 --> 00:54:34.660
Before I got sent away,
I used to sleep anywhere I could,


00:54:34.661 --> 00:54:37.036
like the kitchen,
Mom and Dad's room, outside.


00:54:37.037 --> 00:54:38.412
I slept in the garage
a few times,


00:54:38.413 --> 00:54:41.039
but it only ever got to me


00:54:41.040 --> 00:54:43.542
when I would
try to sleep in beds.


00:54:43.543 --> 00:54:47.294
It's bound to beds.


00:54:47.295 --> 00:54:48.755
Why?


00:54:48.756 --> 00:54:51.840
I don't know.


00:54:51.841 --> 00:54:53.884
I have theories, I guess.


00:54:53.885 --> 00:54:56.804
Beds are where people
sleep the most,


00:54:56.805 --> 00:54:58.595
so if it usually strikes
when you sleep,


00:54:58.596 --> 00:55:00.515
it makes sense.


00:55:00.516 --> 00:55:02.516
That's where you have
the most dreams


00:55:02.517 --> 00:55:04.644
and nightmares.


00:55:04.645 --> 00:55:06.936
Maybe that's what it looks for.


00:55:06.937 --> 00:55:10.523
Maybe.


00:55:10.524 --> 00:55:13.150
I have another theory, too,


00:55:13.151 --> 00:55:16.237
but you can't freak out.


00:55:16.238 --> 00:55:20.407
Go ahead.


00:55:20.408 --> 00:55:22.241
I read once that you shed


00:55:22.242 --> 00:55:24.827
a lot of dead skin cells
in your bed.


00:55:24.829 --> 00:55:27.120
Like while you sleep,
you know, like,


00:55:27.121 --> 00:55:30.163
your bed is full of dead skin


00:55:30.164 --> 00:55:34.544
and pieces of your body.


00:55:34.545 --> 00:55:37.712
Maybe it starts
by, like, feeding on--


00:55:37.713 --> 00:55:40.048
on your dead flesh
before it, you know...


00:55:40.049 --> 00:55:43.342
Before that's
not good enough anymore.


00:55:43.343 --> 00:55:48.343
Yeah.


00:55:55.855 --> 00:56:00.854
You looking at that old Polaroid?


00:56:01.108 --> 00:56:04.611
Yeah. You know about this?


00:56:04.612 --> 00:56:08.614
Yeah, I found it after you left.


00:56:08.615 --> 00:56:11.366
So that's what it looks like, right?


00:56:11.367 --> 00:56:14.244
That crazy face?


00:56:14.245 --> 00:56:17.370
I guess.


00:56:17.371 --> 00:56:22.334
I never tried to take
another picture after this one, so...


00:56:22.335 --> 00:56:26.545
I did.


00:56:26.546 --> 00:56:28.547
You did?


00:56:28.548 --> 00:56:30.633
Yeah.


00:56:30.634 --> 00:56:32.966
I thought that
if I could prove it was real


00:56:32.967 --> 00:56:37.429
then you'd come back
sooner, you know.


00:56:37.430 --> 00:56:40.015
So I started taking
pictures under the bed,


00:56:40.016 --> 00:56:42.100
staying up late, making noise,


00:56:42.101 --> 00:56:44.060
you know, stuff like that.


00:56:44.061 --> 00:56:49.061
Until one night,
that mist came out of nowhere,


00:56:49.106 --> 00:56:54.107
and it's never gone
away since then.


00:56:57.198 --> 00:57:02.197
Can you sleep?


00:57:53.661 --> 00:57:56.871
Neal? Neal!


00:57:56.872 --> 00:58:01.873
What?


00:58:10.925 --> 00:58:13.137
Run.


00:58:13.138 --> 00:58:14.721
Come on, Paulie, this way!


00:58:18.473 --> 00:58:20.600
<i>- Oh, my God!</i>


00:58:32.361 --> 00:58:34.653
Paulie, that's my old bed!


00:58:42.119 --> 00:58:43.704
Aah!


00:59:02.094 --> 00:59:04.387
You okay?


00:59:04.388 --> 00:59:09.387
No.


00:59:22.695 --> 00:59:24.695
Come on, boys, wake up.


00:59:24.696 --> 00:59:29.697
You been asleep all afternoon.


00:59:33.412 --> 00:59:35.788
What is all that?


00:59:35.789 --> 00:59:37.874
We're gonna try
something new tonight,


00:59:37.875 --> 00:59:40.124
something fun.


00:59:40.125 --> 00:59:42.211
Mr. Evans next door
has offered


00:59:42.212 --> 00:59:44.046
to have you guys
spend the night.


00:59:44.047 --> 00:59:47.672
His boys would love to have
you both for a sleepover.


00:59:47.673 --> 00:59:50.676
You gotta be
fucking joking.


00:59:50.677 --> 00:59:52.719
Neal, come on.


00:59:52.720 --> 00:59:54.679
Dad, didn't you just finish telling us
we need to grow up?


00:59:54.680 --> 00:59:55.847
I mean, what the hell?


00:59:55.848 --> 00:59:57.849
- Neal, stop it.
- They're expecting you anytime,


00:59:57.850 --> 00:59:59.433
so whenever you're ready,
up you come, boys.


00:59:59.434 --> 01:00:02.061
Come on, it's gonna be fun.


01:00:02.062 --> 01:00:03.395
Paulie, you're
not gonna need that.


01:00:03.396 --> 01:00:04.437
Give that to me.
Thank you, honey.


01:00:04.438 --> 01:00:05.772
<i>But, Dad...</i>


01:00:05.773 --> 01:00:07.231
No, she's right, honey.
Come on.


01:00:07.232 --> 01:00:09.359
- Thank you, sweetie. Here.
- It's all right.


01:00:09.360 --> 01:00:10.818
Take this.


01:00:10.819 --> 01:00:12.570
Neal, get up.


01:00:12.571 --> 01:00:17.569
Here you go.
Have fun, honey.


01:00:19.034 --> 01:00:24.033
Be good, please?


01:00:53.272 --> 01:00:55.147
Oh.


01:00:55.148 --> 01:00:56.147
Hey, guys-


01:00:56.148 --> 01:00:57.649
Hey, Cara.


01:00:57.650 --> 01:00:59.901
Is everything okay?


01:00:59.902 --> 01:01:03.863
Hey, boys, glad you took me up
on my offer to come over.


01:01:03.864 --> 01:01:06.322
Well, it just sounded
too good to pass up.


01:01:06.323 --> 01:01:08.117
Hey, there's little Paul.


01:01:08.118 --> 01:01:09.576
Boy, you're really
growing up fast, little man.


01:01:09.577 --> 01:01:11.452
Only not fast enough.


01:01:14.539 --> 01:01:17.083
So you're staying here
with my brothers?


01:01:17.084 --> 01:01:18.584
Yeah.


01:01:18.585 --> 01:01:21.961
I gotta stay close
to Paulie, you know.


01:01:21.962 --> 01:01:26.961
Yeah, I guess.


01:01:38.768 --> 01:01:42.812
Okay, Robert, Richard,
our guests have arrived.


01:01:42.813 --> 01:01:44.188
Okay, yeah.


01:01:44.189 --> 01:01:45.982
Got it.


01:01:45.983 --> 01:01:47.734
Now, uh, they're gonna
be staying all night,


01:01:47.735 --> 01:01:49.818
so you make sure
that they, uh, feel


01:01:49.819 --> 01:01:53.696
like this place
is their home, okay?


01:01:53.697 --> 01:01:58.697
Excuse me.


01:02:01.662 --> 01:02:03.915
Hey, guys.


01:02:03.916 --> 01:02:06.582
Hey. Sorry, we don't
have any extra chairs.


01:02:10.211 --> 01:02:15.048
Is it cool if we just
throw our pillows on your bed?


01:02:23.098 --> 01:02:27.350
Hey, Neal.


01:02:27.351 --> 01:02:28.683
You know how you were talking


01:02:28.684 --> 01:02:33.684
about dead skin cells
on our bed and stuff?


01:02:34.983 --> 01:02:39.981
Well, do you think they could be
on our pillows, too?


01:02:40.613 --> 01:02:43.405
I mean,
I've had this since I was six.


01:02:43.406 --> 01:02:48.159
You think that'd be enough
to get it over here?


01:02:48.160 --> 01:02:52.411
No.


01:02:52.412 --> 01:02:57.413
No way.


01:03:29.737 --> 01:03:32.780
What's going on?


01:03:32.781 --> 01:03:34.739
I was gonna ask you.


01:03:34.740 --> 01:03:36.242
Having fun?


01:03:36.243 --> 01:03:39.827
Time of my life.


01:03:39.828 --> 01:03:42.287
Sorry it was weird,
me being here.


01:03:42.288 --> 01:03:44.581
No, it's okay.


01:03:44.582 --> 01:03:48.210
I just came over here to say
if you get bored with these spazzes,


01:03:48.211 --> 01:03:49.711
you can come down the hall
and find me


01:03:49.712 --> 01:03:51.587
and I can make us some tea.


01:03:51.588 --> 01:03:54.423
We can catch up.


01:03:54.424 --> 01:03:57.759
Yeah, that's cool. Thanks.


01:03:57.760 --> 01:04:01.595
I just have to wait
till Paulie falls asleep, and...


01:04:01.596 --> 01:04:06.596
Cool.


01:04:33.707 --> 01:04:36.667
Ohh.


01:05:34.175 --> 01:05:39.174
Hmm.


01:05:42.349 --> 01:05:44.225
It's a nice TV.


01:05:44.226 --> 01:05:45.601
Yeah.


01:05:45.602 --> 01:05:47.185
Thanks.


01:05:47.186 --> 01:05:50.021
Is it bigger
than the one you guys have?


01:05:50.022 --> 01:05:51.773
We don't have a TV.


01:05:51.774 --> 01:05:54.398
What the hell
do you mean, you don't have a TV?


01:05:54.399 --> 01:05:57.110
We just don't, that's all.


01:05:57.111 --> 01:06:00.822
Our dad took it away
a few years ago.


01:06:00.823 --> 01:06:04.242
Was it TV that made you
go all, you know?


01:06:04.243 --> 01:06:07.577
No, it wasn't, because...


01:06:07.578 --> 01:06:10.329
It's cool, Paul.


01:06:10.330 --> 01:06:13.375
No, actually,
nobody knew at the time,


01:06:13.376 --> 01:06:15.625
so they just got rid of it.


01:06:15.626 --> 01:06:18.294
Better safe than sorry.


01:06:18.295 --> 01:06:19.461
So it's true that
they took you away


01:06:19.462 --> 01:06:21.172
to the prison
for the criminally insane?


01:06:21.173 --> 01:06:22.965
Why do you have to be
such a jerk like that?


01:06:22.966 --> 01:06:24.801
We have the right
to know who's in our house.


01:06:24.802 --> 01:06:26.552
Everybody's talking about it.


01:06:26.553 --> 01:06:28.554
They say you disappeared
after your mom died.


01:06:28.555 --> 01:06:30.388
And you tried to burn
the house down.


01:06:30.389 --> 01:06:32.932
So maybe I did.


01:06:32.933 --> 01:06:34.307
What the hell's with that?


01:06:34.308 --> 01:06:37.602
I mean, what happened
to your brain?


01:06:37.603 --> 01:06:38.812
Do you really want to know?


01:06:38.813 --> 01:06:40.480
Neal, let's not talk about that.


01:06:40.481 --> 01:06:45.479
Do you two really want to know?


01:06:46.236 --> 01:06:47.569
Then pause your movie.


01:06:47.570 --> 01:06:49.904
These lights are going off.


01:07:02.791 --> 01:07:04.041
Terry?


01:07:04.042 --> 01:07:06.669
Yeah, yeah! I got it!


01:07:06.670 --> 01:07:11.669
God damn it.


01:07:42.618 --> 01:07:46.536
God!


01:08:14.101 --> 01:08:17.104
Oh, Terry!


01:08:17.105 --> 01:08:22.103
What are you doing?


01:08:25.237 --> 01:08:28.447
Terry?


01:08:28.448 --> 01:08:31.240
Ouch, jeez.


01:08:31.241 --> 01:08:32.407
Oh!


01:08:35.702 --> 01:08:38.705
Oh, my God.


01:08:57.222 --> 01:08:59.054
I tried to kill it with fire.


01:08:59.055 --> 01:09:02.391
Give me a break.


01:09:02.392 --> 01:09:04.268
The fire took down
most of our house,


01:09:04.269 --> 01:09:07.687
and it even got my mom.


01:09:07.688 --> 01:09:11.399
But that's not
what's really scary.


01:09:11.400 --> 01:09:14.110
What's really scary
is that it survived.


01:09:14.111 --> 01:09:15.903
What did?


01:09:15.904 --> 01:09:17.695
Some crazy guy?


01:09:17.696 --> 01:09:22.283
Not a man, not a human.


01:09:22.284 --> 01:09:23.826
Something that you can't see


01:09:23.827 --> 01:09:26.036
and you can't read about.


01:09:26.037 --> 01:09:27.454
You can only hear about it


01:09:27.455 --> 01:09:31.040
or learn about it
as it attacks you.


01:09:31.041 --> 01:09:34.459
And now Paulie's
getting attacked.


01:09:34.460 --> 01:09:36.087
Paul, show them.


01:09:36.088 --> 01:09:37.212
No, Neal.


01:09:37.213 --> 01:09:42.212
Paul, show them.


01:09:55.061 --> 01:09:56.229
Whatever!


01:09:56.230 --> 01:09:58.355
You could have
done that to him!


01:09:58.356 --> 01:10:00.856
I would never do that
to my brother.


01:10:00.857 --> 01:10:03.276
Neal, this is stupid.
Let's just leave.


01:10:03.277 --> 01:10:06.445
Yeah, you two go find
something fake to hide from.


01:10:06.446 --> 01:10:09.197
Yeah, take your crazy
somewhere else.


01:10:09.198 --> 01:10:11.867
What's the matter, boys?


01:10:11.868 --> 01:10:15.161
You afraid of what might be living
right next door to you?


01:10:15.162 --> 01:10:17.329
Yeah, you and your cuckoo bird
fuckin' brother


01:10:17.330 --> 01:10:20.081
ready to burn our house down.


01:10:20.082 --> 01:10:21.374
Paul, what did you say


01:10:21.375 --> 01:10:26.375
that thing felt like
when it grabbed you?


01:10:27.005 --> 01:10:29.464
He said it felt
icy cold and numb


01:10:29.465 --> 01:10:31.508
like a dead arm
grasping at you.


01:10:31.509 --> 01:10:34.428
I never said that.


01:10:34.429 --> 01:10:39.015
You feel your body
start to fall asleep.


01:10:39.016 --> 01:10:40.265
That's how it likes its food,


01:10:40.266 --> 01:10:44.686
immobile, but still alive.


01:10:44.687 --> 01:10:47.189
It attacks you while you sleep.


01:10:47.190 --> 01:10:52.189
If you move,
if you make a sound,


01:10:52.860 --> 01:10:53.943
if you get too close...


01:10:55.445 --> 01:10:57.364
It's too late for you.


01:10:57.365 --> 01:11:00.240
Yeah, right. If you believe that,


01:11:00.241 --> 01:11:02.576
you're even crazier
than anyone could guess.


01:11:02.577 --> 01:11:04.328
I wouldn't wish believing in this


01:11:04.329 --> 01:11:09.123
on my worst fucking enemy,
including you two.


01:11:09.124 --> 01:11:10.583
Neal?


01:11:10.584 --> 01:11:11.834
Paul, come on, what is it?


01:11:11.835 --> 01:11:13.668
Look at their floor.


01:11:20.258 --> 01:11:23.343
Wh-what's this stuff? Fog?


01:11:23.344 --> 01:11:24.929
Hey, is this some kind of a joke?


01:11:24.930 --> 01:11:29.929
GUYS, guys, Shh!


01:11:30.141 --> 01:11:31.975
Uh, it's just mist from outside.


01:11:31.976 --> 01:11:33.728
Knock it off!


01:11:33.729 --> 01:11:38.189
Don't talk!


01:11:38.190 --> 01:11:40.984
Guys, stop!


01:11:40.985 --> 01:11:42.526
Don't move.


01:11:42.527 --> 01:11:44.236
Don't make a sound.


01:11:56.247 --> 01:11:57.288
Paulie, run!


01:11:57.289 --> 01:11:58.373
Aah! Aah!


01:11:59.375 --> 01:12:00.500
Aah! Neal!


01:12:09.508 --> 01:12:10.508
Aah!


01:12:11.885 --> 01:12:16.513
Mom! Dad! Help!


01:12:18.057 --> 01:12:20.016
<i>- Aah! </i>


01:12:23.145 --> 01:12:24.603
Cara, stop! Don't move!


01:12:24.604 --> 01:12:25.979
You're in the light!


01:12:25.980 --> 01:12:27.065
As fast as you can,
run to your room,


01:12:27.066 --> 01:12:28.442
turn the light on,


01:12:28.443 --> 01:12:29.775
and don't come out
no matter what you hear!


01:12:29.776 --> 01:12:31.067
What about you?


01:12:31.068 --> 01:12:32.402
I'm going after my brother!


01:12:32.403 --> 01:12:37.402
Cara, run!


01:12:40.451 --> 01:12:41.659
Okay, it's just me.


01:12:42.704 --> 01:12:43.744
<i>- Dad
Dad!</i>


01:12:43.745 --> 01:12:45.455
- Dad!
- Dad! It's us!


01:12:45.456 --> 01:12:46.622
What the hell's going--


01:12:46.623 --> 01:12:47.999
Close the door!


01:12:48.000 --> 01:12:49.708
What the hell's going on,
you two?


01:12:49.709 --> 01:12:51.419
Were you guys just
in here five minutes ago?


01:12:51.420 --> 01:12:52.752
No, Dad! We have to get
out of this house!


01:12:52.753 --> 01:12:53.795
We have to leave right now!


01:12:53.796 --> 01:12:54.920
Was one of you walking around


01:12:54.921 --> 01:12:56.713
all wrapped up
in a sheet or not, damn it?


01:12:56.714 --> 01:12:58.549
No, no, no!
That's the thing that's after us!


01:12:58.550 --> 01:13:00.216
You guys are
just little monsters!


01:13:00.217 --> 01:13:02.177
I've done nothing
but try to be nice to you!


01:13:02.178 --> 01:13:05.596
Angela! We're sorry,
but you have to listen to us now!


01:13:05.597 --> 01:13:07.140
- Listen to you? How can I...
- We have to get out of this house!


01:13:07.141 --> 01:13:10.476
- We have to leave right now!
- Listen to you?!


01:13:12.144 --> 01:13:13.936
Run!


01:13:13.937 --> 01:13:15.188
Get down! Get down!


01:13:15.189 --> 01:13:19.316
Aah! No! No! Honey, no!


01:13:19.317 --> 01:13:21.569
Aah!


01:13:21.570 --> 01:13:23.527
Aah!


01:13:23.528 --> 01:13:25.237
Dad!


01:13:25.238 --> 01:13:27.073
Aah!


01:13:27.074 --> 01:13:28.073
Dad!


01:13:28.074 --> 01:13:30.202
Aah!


01:13:32.411 --> 01:13:34.330
<i>- Oh my God!
Dad! </i>


01:13:36.916 --> 01:13:37.999
Aah!


01:13:38.000 --> 01:13:42.998
Terry! Terry!


01:13:43.837 --> 01:13:45.339
Paul! Paul, get out of here!


01:13:45.340 --> 01:13:50.339
Get out!


01:14:01.561 --> 01:14:03.728
Angela! Turn the lights on!


01:14:03.729 --> 01:14:07.982
I can't, Neal! The power's off!


01:14:07.983 --> 01:14:09.651
Oh, my God!


01:14:09.652 --> 01:14:11.485
- It's okay.


01:14:11.486 --> 01:14:13.154
It's okay, I'm here.


01:14:13.155 --> 01:14:14.488
It got Dad!


01:14:14.489 --> 01:14:16.323
- Oh, my God.
- I know.


01:14:16.324 --> 01:14:17.407
It's not afraid of us, Neal.


01:14:17.408 --> 01:14:19.909
It's not afraid.


01:14:19.910 --> 01:14:21.619
It's not gonna get us!


01:14:21.620 --> 01:14:23.829
Angela, are you okay?


01:14:23.830 --> 01:14:26.373
What is that thing?


01:14:26.374 --> 01:14:28.332
We need to get
out of this house right now!


01:14:28.333 --> 01:14:30.709
We need to move quickly and quietly
and get out the front door.


01:14:30.710 --> 01:14:34.713
There's more lights by the street.


01:14:34.714 --> 01:14:39.634
I'm gonna open the door,
and then we're gonna move.


01:14:39.634 --> 01:14:44.635
Angela, you first,
then you, Paulie, then me.


01:14:45.431 --> 01:14:46.973
Get ready.


01:15:00.529 --> 01:15:02.112
Paulie, look out!


01:15:02.113 --> 01:15:04.071
Aah!


01:15:04.072 --> 01:15:05.155
Aah!


01:15:05.156 --> 01:15:06.700
Neal! Neal, help!


01:15:06.701 --> 01:15:08.158
Aah!


01:15:08.159 --> 01:15:11.911
Neal! Neal, no!


01:15:11.912 --> 01:15:12.912
Paulie!


01:15:12.913 --> 01:15:14.079
Paulie! Paulie!


01:15:14.080 --> 01:15:16.081
Take me! Take me!


01:15:16.082 --> 01:15:17.666
Paulie!


01:15:17.667 --> 01:15:21.335
Paulie!


01:15:21.336 --> 01:15:22.379
Oh, my God!


01:15:22.380 --> 01:15:24.547
Angela, listen to me!
Listen to me, please!


01:15:24.548 --> 01:15:27.633
This thing has been
after me for two years.


01:15:27.634 --> 01:15:29.467
If it wanted Paulie,
it would have taken him a long time ago.


01:15:29.468 --> 01:15:30.970
It just wants me.


01:15:30.971 --> 01:15:33.053
It's using Paulie
as bait to get to me.


01:15:33.054 --> 01:15:35.432
But if I don't go after him now,
it's gonna be too late.


01:15:35.433 --> 01:15:37.182
No, no, Neal, no!


01:15:37.183 --> 01:15:38.851
No, I think I can find
a way to get to it,


01:15:38.852 --> 01:15:40.810
but I--I need
your help, please.


01:15:40.811 --> 01:15:43.021
Angela, I can't do this without you.


01:15:43.022 --> 01:15:45.481
I need you. I need your help.


01:15:45.482 --> 01:15:46.983
Okay, okay, okay.


01:15:46.984 --> 01:15:49.652
What do you want me to do?


01:15:49.653 --> 01:15:54.651
Get some rope.


01:16:05.458 --> 01:16:08.417
Okay, Angela,
I'm gonna do this.


01:16:08.418 --> 01:16:10.794
Come here.


01:16:11.837 --> 01:16:15.089
Good luck, sweetheart.


01:16:15.090 --> 01:16:16.716
Come back to me, okay?


01:16:16.717 --> 01:16:19.635
Oh, and, Neal...


01:16:19.636 --> 01:16:21.053
no matter what happens,


01:16:21.054 --> 01:16:23.137
I will not let go
of this fucking rope!


01:16:23.138 --> 01:16:27.265
You hear me?


01:16:27.266 --> 01:16:32.266
Go, go, hurry!


01:17:31.531 --> 01:17:32.864
Paulie!?


01:17:39.787 --> 01:17:44.164
Oh, no. Shit!


01:17:53.047 --> 01:17:55.132
Paulie?


01:18:08.060 --> 01:18:09.269
Paulie?


01:18:20.404 --> 01:18:24.531
Neal!


01:18:24.532 --> 01:18:25.949
Neal!


01:18:33.624 --> 01:18:37.000
I can't believe it!


01:18:37.001 --> 01:18:40.044
I told you we were
in this shit together, didn't I?


01:18:40.045 --> 01:18:41.129
Where are we, Neal?


01:18:41.130 --> 01:18:43.673
I don't know.


01:18:43.674 --> 01:18:45.340
Why are we in hell?


01:18:45.341 --> 01:18:46.967
What did we do wrong?


01:18:46.968 --> 01:18:48.677
We're not, Paulie.
We're still alive,


01:18:48.678 --> 01:18:52.013
and I need you to keep it
together with me, okay?


01:18:52.014 --> 01:18:53.973
Angela's still got the other end
of this back in the bedroom.


01:18:53.974 --> 01:18:55.557
She's not gonna let go.


01:18:55.558 --> 01:18:59.103
Dad's dead. He's gone.


01:18:59.104 --> 01:19:02.522
Yeah, Paulie, he's gone.


01:19:02.523 --> 01:19:05.066
But we're gonna live
to remember him


01:19:05.067 --> 01:19:09.861
just like Mom.


01:19:21.748 --> 01:19:25.666
Come on, Paulie!
Hurry, hurry!


01:19:25.667 --> 01:19:26.834
Look, Paulie, there's the rope.


01:19:26.835 --> 01:19:27.835
You can reach it, all right?


01:19:27.836 --> 01:19:30.046
- I'm gonna hold you up!
- No, no! I can't reach that!


01:19:30.047 --> 01:19:31.671
Paulie, you can do this, okay?


01:19:31.672 --> 01:19:36.672
I need you to do this!


01:19:37.344 --> 01:19:42.344
Unh! Come on, Paulie!


01:19:43.975 --> 01:19:48.974
- Shit!


01:19:49.230 --> 01:19:51.939
Oh, my God! Oh, honey!


01:19:51.940 --> 01:19:54.232
Oh, my God!
It's good to see you!


01:19:54.233 --> 01:19:55.776
Oh, Neal!


01:19:55.777 --> 01:19:57.402
Oh, God!


01:19:57.403 --> 01:20:02.401
Oh, thank...thank you!


01:20:27.637 --> 01:20:30.763
Neal! Oh, my God!


01:20:30.764 --> 01:20:32.516
They're all dead!


01:20:32.517 --> 01:20:35.977
Oh, my God!


01:20:45.067 --> 01:20:46.067
Die!


01:20:46.068 --> 01:20:51.069
Come!


01:21:05.127 --> 01:21:07.503
Oh! Oh!


01:21:07.504 --> 01:21:09.296
- Come on!


01:21:16.302 --> 01:21:17.428
Die!


01:21:17.429 --> 01:21:19.804
Aah!


01:21:22.808 --> 01:21:25.727
No, Paulie!


01:21:39.989 --> 01:21:42.283
Neal, the ashes!


01:21:42.284 --> 01:21:47.282
Mom!


01:21:49.040 --> 01:21:54.038
Aaaah!


01:22:08.555 --> 01:22:09.555
Unh!

